From 3e8ceffc10c20fa0f983557eb94978e0dc9162d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 19:55:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] VC4: the ECAT-VC4-ODM1 vacuum module gets its own branch (4
 VCs; make vacuum on the EVEN channel, as measured), the ECAT-VC8 unchanged
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The modules on ring 1 stations 160 / 161 / 162 report "ECAT-VC4-ODM1" (VendorID 0x00494350, ProductID 0x00A20401; card map DI 9 /
DO 3 bytes). EastSun 20261001 measured: "開真空是16bit 破真空17bit ... 開真空是22bit 破真空23bit" (VC n: make 16+2n, break 17+2n --
the opposite parity of the VC8 manual) and ruled "VC8 和 VC4 要不同分支".
EtherCAT/Pci1203Vc8.h: the identity table returns a model (ECAT-VC8 / ECAT-VC4 with ICP's VendorID); per-model layout (VCs 8/4, DI
bytes 17/9, vacuum-OK base 128/64, DO 16..31 / 16..23, SDO VC 0..7 / 0..3, make parity odd / even); new *For checks. The route
(Pci1203Vc8Route.inc) and Pci1203Control's re-check use the station's model; VC4 SDO writes are refused unless
W906_VC4_SDO_WRITE (Pci1203Vc8.h, off: the VC4 object dictionary is unverified); SDO reads allowed.
Panels (MyVacuumPanel): on a VC4 the make / break / OK channels come from the VC (16+2VC / 17+2VC / 64+VC), golden's ports
otherwise; a refused VC4 mode write does not set golden's Error5 (deviation, recorded).
Sucker gate (Vc8Route.h): each registered alias carries its role and Port; on a VC4 a row must have the sensor at 64..67, _On even
and _Off odd in 16..23 and the DO pair on the sensor's VC -- today's VC8-style IO_Table rows on 160..162 are therefore refused (the
IO_Table proposal is in the work log, pending EastSun). VC8 rules unchanged.
Tests: VacuumVc8 (identity -> model, both layouts, VC4 panel writes 20 / 21 and reads 66, SDO write refused, gate cases; every VC8
check unchanged). pci1203_readonly_gate PASS; pci1203_control_gate VC8 checks pass (its 2 old FAILs are elsewhere).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
